        "texto": "See also Proverbs 25: 24. It is customary to build on the flat roofs of Eastern houses arbors, or booths (called “tabernacles” in Matt. 17:4) for the purpose of resting from the heat of the day during the summer. They are also occupied as sleeping-chambers at night. Some suppose…",
